return [
    'enric-mas-the-triumph-of-perseverance' => [
        'slug' => 'enric-mas-the-triumph-of-perseverance', 'title' => 'Enric Mas: The Triumph of Perseverance', 'category' => 'Pro Cycling', 'date' => 'September 15, 2026',
        'thumbnail' => 'images/7/3/3.png', 'hero' => 'https://gobik.com/cdn/shop/articles/TOP_BANNER_02_cb5320e4-8ef8-4178-9315-dbb16321380c.jpg?v=1789483886&width=1100',
        'blocks' => [$p('Enric Mas first stood on the podium of La Vuelta a España in 2018. Just 23 years old, he finished second in Madrid and established himself as one of Spanish cycling’s most promising Grand Tour contenders. In the years that followed, he remained a consistent presence near the top of the general classification, but an overall victory continued to elude him.'), $p('In Granada, that changed. At 31, the Movistar Team rider claimed his first Grand Tour victory, winning La Vuelta a España 2026 after three demanding weeks of racing against some of the strongest riders in the peloton.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/01_a3e0e7d1-4c2a-4637-aeea-c174d31e8d33.jpg?v=1789479018'), $p('For Mas, the result represented the culmination of years spent pursuing the same objective. His career had become closely associated with La Vuelta, a race in which he repeatedly demonstrated the ability to compete with the world’s best without quite reaching the top step.'), $p('The 2026 edition initially appeared to offer another formidable challenge. Tadej Pogačar entered among the leading favorites and made his intentions clear from the opening stages, attacking aggressively whenever the terrain offered an opportunity.'), $p('Stage six, between Alcossebre and Castelló, provided an early indication that Mas might be capable of changing the narrative. On the climb to El Bartolo, Pogačar accelerated away from the favorites. Mas responded, closed the gap, and reached the summit alongside him.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/02_048ee93f-ecfa-423b-bfef-5db540631b4e.jpg?v=1789479020'), $p('Although Pogačar won the stage in the sprint, Mas had demonstrated that he could match one of cycling’s most explosive riders on decisive terrain. The performance suggested that Movistar’s ambitions could extend beyond another podium finish.'), $p('Two days later, the race changed dramatically when Pogačar crashed and abandoned. Mas inherited the race lead and the red jersey, but the greatest challenge was still ahead: defending that advantage through nearly two weeks of mountainous racing.'), $p('He responded immediately, winning the following stage to Alto de Aitana and strengthening his position in the general classification. From that point forward, his race became one of discipline, consistency, and calculated defense.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/03_1f004f6b-16f9-473c-8099-63bbade5f3a7.jpg?v=1789479016'), $p('As the final week unfolded, Primož Roglič, Felix Gall, and the remaining contenders attempted to reduce the deficit. Mas answered each significant challenge, relying on his climbing consistency and the collective strength of Movistar Team.'), $p('Stage 20 offered the final major examination. With nearly 5,000 meters of accumulated climbing, the route demanded both endurance and tactical control. Mas not only protected his lead but extended his advantage over Roglič to two minutes and fifteen seconds.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/04-05_UNITED.jpg?v=1789479023'), $heading('A Victory Years in the Making'), $p('By the final stage in Granada, the overall result was effectively settled. Mas crossed the finish line as the winner of La Vuelta a España, securing the first Grand Tour title of his career.'), $p('The victory carried significance beyond the result itself. Years of near misses, repeated podium finishes, and sustained performances had finally produced the outcome he had pursued since emerging as a young contender in 2018.'), $p('It was also a collective achievement. Movistar Team spent the race controlling the peloton, protecting its leader, and responding to the challenges of rival teams. Their work transformed an individual opportunity into a defining result.'), $p('For Mas, the red jersey was more than a symbol of three successful weeks. It represented the persistence required to remain competitive at the highest level, season after season, until opportunity and preparation finally aligned.')],
    ],
    'sea-otter-europe-2026' => [
        'slug' => 'sea-otter-europe-2026', 'title' => 'Sea Otter Europe 2026: A Celebration of Cycling Community', 'category' => 'Events', 'date' => 'September 23, 2026', 'thumbnail' => 'images/7/2/2.png', 'hero' => 'https://gobik.com/cdn/shop/articles/SEA_OTTER_BANNER_01_78e8cae9-d638-4997-b710-b3de4291b9e8.jpg?v=1790227546&width=1100',
        'blocks' => [$p('Each September, Girona becomes a gathering place for riders, brands, teams and cycling enthusiasts from across Europe. Sea Otter Europe 2026 continued that tradition, bringing together competitive racing, new equipment, community experiences and the culture surrounding the sport.'), $p('Across the weekend, visitors explored new collections, met professional teams and took part in activities that extended well beyond the exhibition stands. Movistar Team, Klimatiza Orbea Team, 226ERS and Canyon were among the names contributing to the atmosphere.'), $heading('Beyond the Exhibition'), $p('One of the defining characteristics of Sea Otter Europe is the opportunity for direct interaction between the cycling industry and the people who ride its products. Professional athletes, recreational cyclists and curious newcomers share the same space, creating conversations that rarely happen in a conventional retail environment.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/SEA_OTTER_BANNER_02.jpg?v=1790172787'), $p('Throughout the event, visitors could attend a Q&A with the Movistar Gravel Squad, participate in a track-stand balance challenge alongside Klimatiza Orbea Team, and explore creative activities including live tote-bag customization and temporary tattoos.'), $p('These smaller experiences helped make the event feel less like a conventional trade show and more like a gathering of people connected through cycling.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/SEA_OTTER_BANNER_05.jpg?v=1790176908'), $heading('Racing and Celebration'), $p('Competition remained an important part of the weekend. David Valero delivered one of the event’s headline performances with victory in the Sea Otter Europe UCI Marathon World Cup race, adding to the excitement of an edition reported to have attracted close to 80,000 visitors.'), $p('The weekend also offered an opportunity to celebrate Movistar Team’s recent success at La Vuelta a España. A gathering organized with 226ERS and Canyon brought together riders and supporters for pizza, drinks and a live DJ set.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/SEA_OTTER_BANNER_03.jpg?v=1790172790'), $heading('The Value of Coming Together'), $p('What makes Sea Otter Europe significant is not simply the number of exhibitors or the scale of the racing. It is the concentration of different cycling communities in one place.'), $p('From professional teams and equipment manufacturers to local clubs and everyday riders, the event offers a reminder that cycling is shaped as much by shared experiences as by competition.'), $p('For Girona, another edition reinforced its position as a meeting point for European cycling culture.')],
    ],
    'how-to-dress-for-winter-cycling' => [
        'slug' => 'how-to-dress-for-winter-cycling', 'title' => 'How to Dress for Winter Cycling: A Temperature Guide', 'category' => 'Guides', 'date' => 'October 5, 2026', 'thumbnail' => 'images/7/1/1.png', 'hero' => 'https://gobik.com/cdn/shop/articles/TOP_BANNER_4710f17c-3a3f-4ea1-abe3-4843fbf364f8.jpg?v=1791366241&width=1100',
        'blocks' => [$p('Winter riding presents a different challenge every day. A cold morning can become a mild afternoon, while wind, rain and humidity can make the same temperature feel dramatically different.'), $p('Dressing appropriately is therefore less about wearing as many layers as possible and more about balancing insulation, ventilation and freedom of movement.'), $p('This guide divides winter riding into four practical temperature ranges, with suggested clothing combinations for each.'), $p('Temperature ranges are approximate. Wind, humidity, effort intensity, individual tolerance and ride duration all affect the clothing required.'), $heading('Lightness and Protection for Changing Temperatures'), $p('Adaptable layers for cool mornings and milder afternoons.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/01_Entretiempo.jpg?v=1791366113'), $p('At these temperatures, the challenge is managing changing conditions without overheating. Lightweight jerseys, breathable bib shorts and a thin base layer provide a comfortable starting point.'), $p('A packable vest adds protection during descents or wind-exposed sections and can be removed when the temperature rises.'), $kit('+15 to +20 °C', ['Jersey'=>[$link('VANQUISH','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jerseys-vanquish'),$link('AVALON','https://gobik.com/en/collections/avalon-jerseys')],'Bib shorts'=>[$link('X','https://gobik.com/en/collections/bibs-x')],'Base layer'=>[$link('SECOND SKIN','https://gobik.com/en/collections/baselayers-second-skin')],'Vest'=>[$link('PRIME','https://gobik.com/en/collections/vests-prime')]]), $heading('More Insulation, Without Sacrificing Ventilation'), $p('Additional protection as temperatures begin to fall.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/02_Invierno_suave.jpg?v=1791366113'), $p('As temperatures fall, long-sleeve jerseys and insulating layers become increasingly useful. The goal is to retain warmth at lower intensities while allowing excess heat to escape during harder efforts.'), $p('PACER SOLID, HYDER and WEEZER offer different levels of insulation. Wind-resistant vests such as PLUS and VECTOR add flexibility, while the SELKIE 2.0 jacket provides another option for variable weather.'), $kit('+10 to +15 °C', ['Jersey'=>[$link('PACER SOLID','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jerseys-pacer'),$link('HYDER','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jerseys-hyder'),$link('WEEZER','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jerseys-weezer')],'Vest'=>[$link('PLUS','https://gobik.com/en/collections/vests-plus'),$link('VECTOR','https://gobik.com/en/collections/vests-vector')],'Jacket'=>[$link('SELKIE 2.0','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jackets-selkie')],'Bib shorts'=>[$link('ARTIC STRIDE','https://gobik.com/en/collections/bibs-artic-stride'),$link('LIMITED','https://gobik.com/en/collections/bibs-limited')],'Base layer'=>[$link('CELL SKIN','https://gobik.com/en/collections/baselayers-cell-skin')]]), $heading('More Protection Against Cold and Changing Intensity'), $p('Wind protection and insulation for colder rides.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/03_Invierno_medio.jpg?v=1791366113'), $p('At lower temperatures, wind chill and moisture become more important. Climbing can generate significant heat, while descending exposes the body to rapid cooling.'), $p('Insulated jackets such as ELEMENT, VANTAGE and ENVY 3.0 provide different levels of protection. Thermal bib tights and an appropriate base layer help maintain warmth without restricting movement.'), $kit('+5 to +10 °C', ['Jacket'=>[$link('ELEMENT','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jackets-element'),$link('VANTAGE','https://gobik.com/en/products/jacket-vantage-men-tetsu'),$link('ENVY 3.0','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jackets-envy')],'Vest'=>[$link('EMINENT','https://gobik.com/en/collections/vests-eminent'),$link('ENVY','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jackets-envy')],'Long bib tights'=>[$link('ABSOLUTE','https://gobik.com/en/collections/bibs-absolute'),$link('GRIT','https://gobik.com/en/collections/bibs-grit')],'Base layer'=>[$link('LIMBER SKIN','https://gobik.com/en/collections/baselayers-limber-skin')]]), $heading('Maximum Protection When the Cold Bites'), $p('Thermal layering for demanding winter conditions.'), $image('https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0052/7876/1029/files/04_Invierno_intenso.png?v=1791366114'), $p('When temperatures approach freezing or fall below it, each layer needs a specific purpose. Outerwear should reduce exposure to wind and moisture, insulation should retain warmth, and base layers should help manage perspiration.'), $p('SKIMO PRO, ARMOUR and SUPERARMOUR are options for demanding conditions. SUBZERO thermal tights provide additional wind protection, while insulated gloves, merino socks and overshoes protect exposed extremities.'), $p('The objective is a balanced system rather than excessive layering, since trapped perspiration can become a source of discomfort during long descents.'), $kit('−8 to +5 °C', ['Jacket'=>[$link('SKIMO PRO','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jackets-skimo-pro'),$link('ARMOUR','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jackets-armour'),$link('SUPERARMOUR','https://gobik.com/en/collections/jackets-superarmour')],'Vest'=>[$link('PATHFINDER','https://gobik.com/en/products/vest-pathfinder-unisex-ink-black')],'Long bib tights'=>[$link('SUBZERO','https://gobik.com/en/collections/bibs-subzero')],'Base layer'=>[$link('WINTER MERINO','https://gobik.com/en/collections/baselayers-winter-merino')]]), $heading('One Winter, Different Ways to Prepare'), $p('The same temperature can require very different clothing depending on the route, weather and intensity of the ride.'), $p('Use temperature as a starting point, then adjust your layers to the conditions. A packable vest may be sufficient on a mild morning, while longer winter rides demand greater protection for the body and extremities.'), $p('The right clothing should allow you to focus on the ride rather than the weather.')],
    ],
];
